OL,3,AResidents airlifted to safety after
OL,4,Aflooding in central Chile
OL,5,
OL,6,FPolice in central Chile have airlifted
OL,7,Fseveral residents to safety after
OL,8,Frising floodwaters left them trapped in
OL,9,Ftheir homes.
OL,11,FRecent torrential rains caused the
OL,12,FMapocho river to burst its banks,
OL,13,Fflooding large parts of the city of
OL,14,FTalagante, 35km (22 miles) south-west
OL,15,Fof the capital, Santiago.
OL,17,FSantiago has seen 74mm of rainfall in
OL,18,Fthe first seven days of this month,
OL,19,Fmaking it the rainiest October for the
OL,20,Farea in 76 years, meteorologists have
OL,21,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
